Subject: [PATCH] Distinguish terminal candidate shortfall from transport timeout

A correlated native response completes the transaction even when fewer
measurements are reported than requested. Expose that terminal boundary to
the CLI instead of waiting eight seconds for keys that will never arrive.
Reuse the existing metric timestamp, MID, RUID and count; stamp valid empty
responses too and serialize UnassociatedSTAQuery beside the metric rows.
Validate the complete TLV sequence before replacing the retained snapshot.
No data-model members, tracker semantics, retries or policy are changed.

Under the existing per-AL admission gate, baseline completion before submission
and require a fresh post-submission record with matching metric count. Native
AL/MID correlation remains authoritative; rows and ACK rejections used with a
completion must match its MID/RUID. Return HTTP 503 with success:false,
native_completed:true, retained valid metrics and sorted missing_expected_keys
for a terminal shortfall. Do not invent rejection codes or RCPI values.
Complete responses and genuine ACK rejections retain their existing behavior;
no completion record still uses the unchanged eight-second HTTP 504 timeout.
This establishes the completion contract, not the underlying HAL failure cause.

Upstream-Status: Pending

